<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The shape of a journey ridden on one's own bike, where the rider has said
    that bike is a pedal-assist one (SPEC §7.3, §7.6).

    `illustration_journey_own_bike`, with the bolt of `ic_bike_electric` added
    inside each of the two scaled groups — the same addition, at the same place,
    that `marker_journey_station_electric` makes to the plain station disc. The
    bolt therefore sits exactly where the icon puts it and rides the disc down
    with the glyph, rather than being pinned to a corner.

    The bolt still does not come from the network: it comes from the rider, who
    said what they ride. That is the whole difference from the plain drawing
    beside this one — what the network lends says nothing about a bike that is
    not the network's, and a declared bike says everything about it.

    Mirrored in right-to-left languages, for the reason the other one gives.
-->
